.TH YAZI 1 "October 2026" "Yazi 26.9.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yazi \- terminal file manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yazi
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ ENTRIES ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yazi
opens an interactive terminal file manager rooted at the current working directory. Optional
.I ENTRIES
select the initial file or directory to open.
.PP
For a quick start and configuration information, see
.UR https://yazi-rs.github.io/docs/quick-start
Yazi's quick-start guide
.UE .
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I ENTRIES
Optional paths used to set the current working entry.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --cwd-file " CWD_FILE"
Write the final working directory to
.IR CWD_FILE
on exit.
.TP
.BI --chooser-file " CHOOSER_FILE"
Write selected files to
.I CHOOSER_FILE
when the chooser is opened.
.TP
.BI --client-id " CLIENT_ID"
Use the specified globally unique client ID.
.TP
.BI --local-events " LOCAL_EVENTS"
Report the specified local events to standard output.
.TP
.BI --remote-events " REMOTE_EVENTS"
Report the specified remote events to standard output.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print help and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ya (1)
.br
.UR https://yazi-rs.github.io/docs
Yazi documentation
.UE
.SH AUTHORS
Yazi is developed by the Yazi contributors.
